[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Proposed investment banking relationship",
    "text": "We place tremendous value in our investment banking relationships and view this opportunity as a significant step in providing broad based, high quality investment banking services to Presbyterian Healthcare Services."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Suitability of proposed capabilities",
    "text": "We feel the skills and capacities we I ~ .1 would bring to Presbyterian are well suited to this situation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "Proposed strengths and services",
    "text": "These strengths include: leadership in healthcare finance, extensive experience working with integrated healthcare systems, a teamwork approach, unique idea generation, unparalleled auction rate performance, tailored ll _j derivative products, and a sincere desire to work with Presbyterian."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "Preparedness to provide services",
    "text": "We hope that this proposal helps to demonstrate the commitment and depth of services that we are prepared to provide Presbyterian."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "1. Requested service capabilities",
    "text": "1. I Describe your firm's capabilities and experience in the following key • Re-marketin~; and auction agent services sen·ices and the value that you create for your health care clients. • Counter-party on derivative transactions • Assistance 11·ith merger, acquisition, and divestihire h·ansactions I Developing long-term capital formation strategies Investment banking/underwriting sen·ices • Liquidity and credit support"
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "Full-range investment banking services",
    "text": "Goldman Sachs is a leading global investment banking and securities finn, pro,·iding a full range of investing, I advisory, and financing services worldwide to a substantial and diversified client base, which includes governments, corporations, financial institutions and indi\\·iduals."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "Healthcare group staffing and resources",
    "text": "The finn's Not-for-Profit Healthcare Group consists of 19 fulltime professionals who are supported by members of specialty finance groups such as credit, derivatives, short-term, quantitative and tax services."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "Broad-based client coverage",
    "text": "Goldman Sachs prides itself on providing complete, broad based, intensive coverage for our clients, regardless of where they are in their capital cycle."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "Relationship service standard",
    "text": "We maintain these relationships by providing a complete and varied range of services, by I being a product innovator and market leader, and by focusing on what is best for the client rather than what produces the next trade."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "Business Principles governance",
    "text": "The Firm's Business Principles govern our approach to all of our business activities."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "Client-interests principle",
    "text": "As our Business Principles I indicate, \"Our clients' interests always come first Our experience shows that if we serve our clients welt our own success will follow.\""
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "Finance-team resource duty",
    "text": "Accordingly, finance teams assigned to each particular client are charged with accessing and directing the Firm's vast resources in the structuring and execution of each transaction."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "Integrated delivery system services",
    "text": "Services provided to our integrated delivery system clients on an ongoing basis are similar to those sought by Presbyterian and have included: strategic capital planning, credit strategy, rating agency and investor I relations, capital raising, capital markets/ derivatives implementation, and strategic advisory services."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "Integrated approach to financing",
    "text": "Although each of these clients is unique in its needs and required a customized capital formation strategy, all found that an integrated approach created the greatest level of financing success."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "Capabilities in desired service areas",
    "text": "As explained below, Goldman Sachs is a leader and innovator in each of the service areas desired by Presbyterian: capital formation, underwriting; remarketing; auction agent/broker-dealer services; derivative product development and execution; strategic advisory services; and use of credit enhancement"
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "Integrated expertise and client value",
    "text": "However, as illustrated in the Trinity Healthcare case study which concludes this section, it is through the integration of these areas of expertise into a comprehensive, capital management strategy that we are able to provide our clients with the greatest value."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "Capital Formation Strategies—long view",
    "text": "FORMATION STRATEGI As indicated above, we take the long view of capital formation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "Integrated capital-planning definition",
    "text": "An integrated approach toward capital planning incorporates not only the immediate needs of an organization, but its long-term goals, and includes variables such as the optimal cost of capitat organizational strategic initiatives requiring investment, desired rating category, and asset liability management."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "CSM Model definition",
    "text": "Our Capital Structure Management (CSM) Model is the central tool used in providing this service. The CSM model is a proprietary Monte Carlo simulation-based capital struchlring and optimization system developed specifically for the complex needs of the firm's largest and most prestigious corporate, tax-exempt and sovereign clients."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "Internal use of CSM Model",
    "text": "Goldman Sachs also uses the model internally to evaluate debt and investment strategies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "Optimal portfolio planning",
    "text": "Our model provides CFOs and Treasurers with a plan for constructing optimal debt and investment portfolios based upon their cost/risk objectives and existing constraints."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "Assistance to Presbyterian",
    "text": "The model can assist Presbyterian in determining the type of debt to issue (e.g., maturity, call/put features, fixed versus floating), the exposure of Presbyterian's overall liabilities to movements in interest rates, the impact of derivative securities such as swaps, as well as optimal refunding strategies for existing debt issues."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "Investment and pension-liability capability",
    "text": "It has the capability to evaluate Presbyterian's investment exposures vis-a-vis the debt portfolio and help devise strategies to manage this risk and can incorporate pension liabilities into the overall liability portfolio and assess the impact of the liability on risk management."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "Selective-use limitation",
    "text": "We use this analytical tool for only a select group of clients whose organization and finances are complex and lend"
  }
]

